---
<Service
  slug="blower-door-testing"
  title="Blower Door Testing in Spokane | Bell Energy Solutions"
  description="Third-party blower door air leakage testing for homes by a Retrotec-certified tester in Spokane County and Kootenai County."
  heading="Blower Door Testing"
  lead="Third-party air leakage testing for homes, by a Retrotec-certified tester."
  photo="Blower door set up in a doorway"
>
  <h2>How a blower door test works</h2>
  <p>A blower door fan is sealed into an exterior doorway and used to depressurize or pressurize the building to a set pressure difference, typically 50 pascals. The airflow needed to hold that pressure shows how leaky the building envelope is.</p>
  <p>Results are commonly reported as <span class="term">CFM50</span> (airflow at 50 Pa) and <span class="term">ACH50</span> (air changes per hour at 50 Pa).</p>

  <h2>For Washington builders</h2>
  <p>The Washington State Energy Code requires air leakage testing of new homes. Bell Energy Solutions provides third-party blower door testing.</p>

  <h2>For homeowners</h2>
  <p>A blower door test measures how much air your home leaks.</p>

  <p class="callout">Testing a commercial building? See <a href="/services/commercial-blower-door-testing/">commercial blower door testing</a>, including multi-fan setups.</p>

  <dl class="spec" slot="aside" style="margin-top:20px">
    <div><dt>Certification</dt><dd>Retrotec certified for residential and commercial blower door testing</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Area</dt><dd>{serviceArea.line}</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Pricing</dt><dd>{business.quoteLine}</dd></div>
  </dl>
</Service>
